    {
      "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
      "body": "Withdrawing this blanket validation rule after rechecking current main (`22a89f9`). The standard Docker dependency was updated in #2448 to [zhuzilin/torch_memory_saver@4d525cf](https://github.com/zhuzilin/torch_memory_saver/commit/4d525cf378fdbfe7eb044909b8e66e112a508624), whose “Fix shared stream” change addresses the disabled-allocation IPC failure.\n\nThe fixed `disable()` owns a non-pooled CUDA stream and avoids reusing tracked/VMM blocks in that stream's cache. Its `test/examples/disable_ipc.py` regression pauses tracked allocations, allocates an update tensor inside `disable()`, and successfully exercises `storage._share_cuda_()`. Slime's colocated updater already builds/serializes its fresh flattened bucket inside that disabled region.\n\nThis PR would reject the fixed standard environment unconditionally, so it is no longer an appropriate restriction for current main. Older environments (including the legacy GB10 Docker pin of `torch_memory_saver==0.0.9`) may still need an upgrade or disk transport; this withdrawal does not claim that every historical installation is fixed or close #2188.\n\nThis conclusion is based on the pinned dependency source and upstream regression; I have not run the CUDA IPC test on this local CPU Python environment. The branch and local worktree remain available for historical reference.\n",
